		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>effectivement mon .pgpass n&#039;est pas utilisé ni par barman ni par postgres </p><p>mv /var/lib/barman/.pgpass /var/lib/barman/pgpass.old<br />[root@es7-stkw-dev ~]# systemctl restart postgresql-10.service<br />[root@es7-stkw-dev ~]#&#160; psql -c &#039;SELECT version()&#039; -U barman -h XXXXXXX -d postgres<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;version<br />---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> PostgreSQL 10.4 on x86_64-pc-linux-gnu, compiled by gcc (GCC) 4.8.5 20150623 (Red Hat 4.8.5-28), 64-bit<br />(1 row)</p><p>[root@es7-stkw-dev ~]#&#160; psql -c &#039;SELECT version()&#039; -U postgres -h XXXXXXX -d postgres<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;version<br />---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> PostgreSQL 10.4 on x86_64-pc-linux-gnu, compiled by gcc (GCC) 4.8.5 20150623 (Red Hat 4.8.5-28), 64-bit<br />(1 row)</p><br /><p>la connexion ce fait toujours sans mot de passe</p>]]></content>
